# Wave W17-V (Route 207): relic post — a relic-ring marker post at the switchback bends: a post carrying one pale ring cut into its face, the mark the ring-keepers repaint where the road bends past the relic grass (design: RELICT rings scattered in the foothill grass; the bends are where travellers look for them). On climb turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s banded posts by the ring itself: bands measure and warn, the ring remembers.
